Expected: -50 -> `-0050-01-01`, -1 -> `-0001-01-01`, -1234 -> `-1234-01-01` (already correct), 50 -> `0050-01-01`, 2017 -> `2017-01-01`.

Now check upstream luxon fix. The actual upstream fix was:

```js
export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
  const isNeg = input < 0;
  let padded;
  if (isNeg) {
    padded = "-" + ("" + -input).padStart(n, "0");
  } else {
    padded = ("" + input).padStart(n, "0");
  }
  return padded;
}
```

Wait, but that would give -50 -> "-" + "0050" = "-0050", which has length 5. Hmm. Let's check upstream luxon source. Actually in luxon current master:

```js
export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
  const isNeg = input < 0;
  let padded;
  if (isNeg) {
    padded = "-" + ("" + -input).padStart(n, "0");
  } else {
    padded = ("" + input).padStart(n, "0");
  }
  return padded;
}
```

